/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The A320 has two engine-driven integrated drive generators (IDGs), each rated 90 kVA at 115/200 V, 400 Hz.
   - The APU generator, also 90 kVA, can replace either IDG on the ground or in flight, and ground power plugs in at the nose.
   - The B787 takes no bleed air from its engines.
   - Conversion is spread out.
   - P is real power in watts; Vph is the phase (line-to-neutral) voltage, the 115 V or 235 V quoted for aircraft systems; I is the line current in amperes; cos φ is the power factor.
   - At unity power factor I = P ÷ (3 Vph).
*/
