/* book exam traps: Do not say the B787 needs a constant-speed drive. Its AC bus is variable frequency by design; every load must accept 360-800 Hz. | Do not mix 235 V AC with ±270 V DC. The first is generated and distributed as AC; the second is made from it by ATRUs for large motor loads. | The A320's 115 V is fixed at 400 Hz because the IDG holds generator speed constant; the engine speed itself is not constant. | Generator ratings in kVA are apparent power, not kW. At a power factor below one, the kW available is lower than the kVA rating. | The RAT is an emergency source, not a normal source for engine start or ground power. | Putting 115 V into √3 × V × I. Aircraft quote line-to-neutral voltage: use 3 × 115 × I, or √3 × 200 × I. */
