/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A Bourdon tube is a curved metal tube that straightens as pressure inside rises.
   - Fuel flow is a rate, not a total.
   - Primary indicators are the ones needed to set power safely: N1 fan speed (or engine pressure ratio on some engines), exhaust gas temperature (EGT), and on many types N2 core speed.
   - On a light aircraft the tank has a float on an arm.
   - Transport aircraft use capacitance gauging.
   - C is capacitance in farads (F); ε0 = 8.854 × 10⁻¹² F/m is the permittivity of free space; εr is the relative permittivity of the material between the plates; A is plate area in m²; d is plate separation in m.
   - A real probe is not fully full or fully empty.
   - The tank unit sends capacitance to a bridge.
   - Attitude changes the reading.
   - Fuel flow integration is the cross-check.
*/
